module arwd-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcrimp45.{ frcrimp45 }

// The Western District of Arkansas's own periods in a criminal case under
// the joint Local Rules. L.R. 7.2 governs "all motions" (its (f) names the
// Federal Rules of Criminal Procedure), and its (b) says FRCP 6, including
// 6(d), counts its days; in a criminal case FRCrimP 45(a) computes a
// period "in any local rule", so these count under frcrimp45, whose
// 45(c) adds the three days after service by mail that FRCP 6(d) adds.
// "For cause shown" the court may shorten or lengthen the L.R. 7.2(b)
// times. Stated in the rules but not declared: the summary-judgment reply
// (L.R. 7.2(b), 56.1), a civil motion; the reply of a party seeking relief
// under 28 U.S.C. § 2254 or § 2255 (L.R. 7.2(b)), lit/habeas's; the
// fourteen days to appeal a magistrate judge's referred nondispositive
// ruling and to object to proposed findings and recommendations (L.R.
// 72.1, parts VII.B and VIII.C), which in a criminal case are FRCrimP
// 59(a) and 59(b)(2)'s fourteen days, lit/frcrimp's to state; the
// filing of served papers within seven days (L.R. 5.4), stated under FRCP
// 5(d); and the pro se plaintiff's thirty days (L.R. 5.5(c)(2)), a civil
// rule. Criminal cases are assigned only at random, never as related
// cases (L.R. 40.1(d)), and the Harrison Division's criminal papers are
// filed in Fayetteville (L.R. 5.5(b)(2)); the magistrate judges' misdemeanor, forfeiture of
// collateral, Rule 40 commitment, arraignment, subpoena and dismissal
// duties (L.R. 72.1, parts I-VI) state no period. The earlier W.D. Ark.
// criminal outline's FRCrimP flow and its decisions (Salerno, Brady,
// Barker v. Wingo, Zedner, Boykin, Missouri v. Frye, Jackson v. Virginia,
// Booker, Roe v. Flores-Ortega, Garza v. Idaho) are FRCrimP and
// constitutional authority and belong to lit/frcrimp; no reporter text is
// vendored, so they are removed here, and the court's Speedy Trial Act
// plan (18 U.S.C. § 3165) is not vendored.
/// A motion and its supporting papers are served (L.R. 7.2(b)).
event MotionServed()
/// A magistrate judge takes a reviewable action whose review no law or
/// other local rule provides for (L.R. 72.1, part XI).
event MagistrateActionTaken()

/// L.R. 7.2(b): within fourteen days from the date of service of a motion
/// and its supporting papers, a party opposing it serves and files a
/// concise statement in opposition with supporting authorities. The
/// failure to respond timely to a nondispositive motion is an adequate
/// basis, without more, for granting it (L.R. 7.2(f)).
deadline opposition-period: 14.days after MotionServed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "W.D. Ark. L.R. 7.2(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// L.R. 72.1, part XI.A: a party may file and serve an application for
/// review of a magistrate judge's action, review of which is not
/// otherwise specifically provided for by law or the local rules, not
/// later than fourteen days after it.
deadline magistrate-review-period: 14.days after MagistrateActionTaken() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "W.D. Ark. L.R. 72.1"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

test "opposition period: 14 days after the trigger" cite "W.D. Ark. L.R. 7.2(b)"
{
  given MotionServed() on 2027-03-01
  expect deadline(opposition-period) == 2027-03-15
}

test "magistrate review period: 14 days after the trigger" cite "W.D. Ark. L.R. 72.1"
{
  given MagistrateActionTaken() on 2027-03-01
  expect deadline(magistrate-review-period) == 2027-03-15
}
